# Blog

Purpose: **establish expertise** (React, Next.js, WebSocket, state management, real project lessons) and **SEO**.

## Content Location

```
content/blog/
├── en/
│   └── websocket-trading-state.mdx
└── fa/
    └── websocket-trading-state.mdx   # paired translation (optional but preferred)
```

- Slugs: **kebab-case**, lowercase, English characters
- FA and EN posts on same topic share slug OR link via frontmatter `translationSlug`

## Frontmatter (required)

```yaml
---
title: "Managing Trade State with WebSockets in a Crypto Exchange"
description: "Lessons from building live price feeds and order state on arz.me — without over-engineering."
publishedAt: "2025-03-15"
updatedAt: "2025-03-15"
locale: en
translationSlug: websocket-trading-state   # same slug in other locale folder
tags: [react, websocket, state-management]
draft: false
---
```

| Field | Rules |
|-------|--------|
| `title` | Matches `<h1>`; unique per locale |
| `description` | ≤ 160 chars; used for meta description |
| `publishedAt` | ISO date `YYYY-MM-DD` |
| `draft` | `true` — excluded from build and sitemap |
| `tags` | Lowercase; from allowed set in `content/data/tags.ts` |

## Writing Guidelines

- **Honest, specific, practical** — same voice as `content-branding.mdc`
- Draw from real projects (arz.me, e-commerce panels, Techsnovel) — no fabricated war stories
- Code examples: TypeScript, minimal, runnable context
- Length: **800–2000 words** for pillar posts; shorter notes OK for tips
- EN and FA posts are **independent prose** — not literal translation; same facts and code

## Suggested Initial Topics

1. WebSocket + trade state patterns (from exchange work)
2. Redux vs Zustand in multi-panel e-commerce
3. Building offline-capable PWAs with Next.js
4. SignalR real-time chat patterns (Techsnovel)
5. What I learned moving toward NestJS (honest full-stack path)

## MDX Features

Allowed shortcodes/components:

- `<Callout type="info|warning">` — tips and caveats
- Code blocks with language tag
- Internal links: `/en/projects/arz-me` style
- External links: full URL with `rel="noopener noreferrer"`

Do **not** embed scripts, iframes, or tracking pixels in MDX.

## Blog Index Page

- Sort by `publishedAt` descending
- Filter by tag optional (phase 2) — structure data to allow it
- PostCard: title, description excerpt, date, tags, reading time estimate

## Reading Time

```ts
const words = content.split(/\s+/).length;
const minutes = Math.ceil(words / 200);
```

Display via i18n: `t('blog.readingTime', { minutes })`

## RSS (recommended)

- `frontend/app/[locale]/blog/feed.xml/route.ts` or root `feed.xml`
- Include EN and FA feeds or combined with `language` tags

## SEO

- Each post: `BlogPosting` JSON-LD — see `seo.mdc`
- OG image: default site OG or per-post `ogImage` frontmatter field
- Canonical URL includes locale prefix

## Do Not

- Publish empty placeholder posts with `draft: false`
- Copy-paste documentation without personal angle
- Use AI-slop phrases ("In today's fast-paced world", "Let's dive in") — write direct openings
